WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.587
Test-PaInventory turns those rows
into the nine findings on the slide.

2
00:00:04.587 --> 00:00:09.360
Two thresholds come straight from Learn:
fewer than five Global Administrators,

3
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.138
and no more than three
owners on a subscription.

4
00:00:12.138 --> 00:00:14.117
Learn also backs the biggest one,

5
00:00:14.117 --> 00:00:18.665
standing privilege in the top tiers
outside a short, owned exceptions list,

6
00:00:18.665 --> 00:00:22.259
and the root-scope finding,
because elevating access hands

7
00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:26.000
someone User Access Administrator
over every subscription.

8
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.045
The rest are the program's own design,
labeled that way: roles assigned straight

9
00:00:31.045 --> 00:00:36.070
to people, badly named groups, unmapped
roles, and eligibility that never ends.
